w: An- gels we have heard on high Sweet- ly sing- ing o'er the plains,
w: Shep- herds, why this ju- bi- lee? Why your joy- ous strains pro- long?
w: Come to Beth- le- hem and see Christ Whose birth the an- gels sing;
w: See Him in a man- ger laid, Whom the choirs of an- gels praise;
A A A c | c3/2 B/ A2 | A G A c | A3/2 G/ F2 |
w: And the moun- tains in re- ply E- cho- ing their joy- ous strains.
w: What the glad- some ti- dings be Which in- spire your heav'n- ly song?
w: Come, a- dore on bend- ed knee, Christ the Lord, the new- born King.
w: Ma- ry, Jo- seph, lend your aid, While our hearts in love we raise.
